.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd October 28, 2026
.Dt NOQTIS-VERIFY 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm noqtis-verify
.Nd check an ML-DSA or SLH-DSA signature of a file
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm noqtis verify
.Fl p Ar key.pub
.Fl s Ar sig
.Op Fl c Ar ctx
.Op Fl -ph Ar hash
.Op Fl q
.Ar file
.Nm noqtis verify
.Fl p Ar key.pub
.Fl -dsse
.Op Fl o Ar payload
.Op Fl q
.Ar envelope
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm noqtis verify
checks that
.Ar sig
is a valid signature of the bytes of
.Ar file
under the public key in
.Ar key.pub .
On success it prints
.Dl <file>: OK (<alg>)
On failure it prints to standard error why
.Po
.Dq the signature does not verify ,
or the signature's length when it is not the algorithm's
.Pc .
.Ar file
may be
.Ql -
for standard input.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl p Ar key.pub , Fl -pub Ns = Ns Ar key.pub
A public signature key file
.Pq Ql noqtis-key-1 <alg> pub .
The algorithm comes from the key file.
.It Fl s Ar sig , Fl -sig Ns = Ns Ar sig
The raw signature.
.It Fl c Ar ctx , Fl -ctx Ns = Ns Ar ctx
The context string the signer used (at most 255 bytes; default empty).
.It Fl -ph Ar hash
Verify a pre-hash (HashML-DSA, HashSLH-DSA) signature made with
.Ar hash ;
the names are those of
.Xr noqtis-sign 1 .
.It Fl q , Fl -quiet
Print nothing on success; only the exit status tells.
.It Fl -dsse
Check a DSSE envelope
.Pq Xr noqtis-export 1 Fl -as Cm dsse
instead: one of its signatures must verify under
.Ar key.pub
over the envelope's pre-authentication encoding; then
.Ql <envelope>: OK (<alg>), payloadType <type>
is printed.
.It Fl o Ar payload , Fl -out Ns = Ns Ar payload
With
.Fl -dsse :
write the envelope's payload to
.Ar payload .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 3n -compact
.It 0
The signature is valid.
.It 1
It is not: a wrong signature, file, key, context or pre-hash, or a
signature of the wrong length.
.It 2
A usage error, a key that is not a public signature key, or a file that
cannot be read.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ noqtis verify -p me.pub -s report.pdf.sig report.pdf
report.pdf: OK (ML-DSA-65)
$ echo changed >> report.pdf
$ noqtis verify -p me.pub -s report.pdf.sig report.pdf; echo $?
noqtis verify: report.pdf: FAILED: the signature does not verify
1
.Ed
.Pp
In a script:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
if noqtis verify -q -p me.pub -s data.sig data.csv; then
  echo trusted
fi
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-export 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-sign 1 ,
.Xr nqdsse 3 ,
.Xr nqsign 3
